a-start=3D"0" data-end=3D"181" class=3D"" style=3D"">You can clean the Cano=
n iR 2002 fuser, but only the accessible surfaces. Do not disassemble the f=
user unless you are trained=E2=80=94the heater uses mains voltage and becom=
es extremely hot.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"183" data-end=3D"210" data-section-id=3D"wskkxr">Safe cle=
aning procedure</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"212" data-end=3D"759">
<li data-start=3D"212" data-end=3D"263" data-section-id=3D"twhrxg">
<p data-start=3D"215" data-end=3D"263">Turn off the printer with the main p=
ower switch.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"264" data-end=3D"290" data-section-id=3D"1aftrnx">
<p data-start=3D"267" data-end=3D"290">Unplug the power cable.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"291" data-end=3D"348" data-section-id=3D"1bs6vmy">
<p data-start=3D"294" data-end=3D"348">Wait at least <strong data-start=3D"=
308" data-end=3D"325">30=E2=80=9345 minutes</strong> for the fuser to cool.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"349" data-end=3D"428" data-section-id=3D"1qdxxwh">
<p data-start=3D"352" data-end=3D"428">Open the rear/right cover and locate=
 the fixing unit in the paper-exit path.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"429" data-end=3D"468" data-section-id=3D"13u0wf9">
<p data-start=3D"432" data-end=3D"468">Remove loose paper scraps carefully.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"469" data-end=3D"626" data-section-id=3D"1itd7h">
<p data-start=3D"472" data-end=3D"519">Wipe accessible paper guides and rol=
lers using:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"524" data-end=3D"626">
<li data-start=3D"524" data-end=3D"549" data-section-id=3D"fiojm9">
<p data-start=3D"526" data-end=3D"549">A soft, lint-free cloth</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"553" data-end=3D"589" data-section-id=3D"1vlkju8">
<p data-start=3D"555" data-end=3D"589">Slightly dampened with clean water</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"593" data-end=3D"626" data-section-id=3D"1ci3j5k">
<p data-start=3D"595" data-end=3D"626">A dry lint-free cloth afterward</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"628" data-end=3D"686" data-section-id=3D"nmogd0">
<p data-start=3D"631" data-end=3D"686">Rotate only rollers that turn easily=
. Never force them.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"687" data-end=3D"759" data-section-id=3D"1x4700u">
<p data-start=3D"690" data-end=3D"759">Let everything dry completely, close=
 the covers, and reconnect power.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"761" data-end=3D"788" data-section-id=3D"1lcn0un">Cleanin=
g the thermistor</h3>
<p data-start=3D"790" data-end=3D"888">Cleaning the thermistor requires rem=
oving and opening the fuser. This is normally technician work:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"890" data-end=3D"1241">
<li data-start=3D"890" data-end=3D"918" data-section-id=3D"15s05lc">
<p data-start=3D"892" data-end=3D"918">Remove the fuser assembly.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"919" data-end=3D"938" data-section-id=3D"1klgazh">
<p data-start=3D"921" data-end=3D"938">Open its housing.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"939" data-end=3D"1008" data-section-id=3D"18wklwy">
<p data-start=3D"941" data-end=3D"1008">Locate the small thermistor contact=
ing the fixing film/heater area.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1009" data-end=3D"1112" data-section-id=3D"9dwrci">
<p data-start=3D"1011" data-end=3D"1112">Carefully remove baked toner using=
 a lint-free swab and a small amount of <strong data-start=3D"1085" data-en=
d=3D"1111">90%+ isopropyl alcohol</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1113" data-end=3D"1177" data-section-id=3D"g5iqlc">
<p data-start=3D"1115" data-end=3D"1177">Do not bend, scratch, reposition, =
or press hard on the sensor.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1178" data-end=3D"1241" data-section-id=3D"1ivdkr1">
<p data-start=3D"1180" data-end=3D"1241">Inspect the thermistor cable and c=
onnector before reassembly.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1243" data-end=3D"1262" data-section-id=3D"69vxjw">Do not=
 do these</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1264" data-end=3D"1571">
<li data-start=3D"1264" data-end=3D"1307" data-section-id=3D"10a8xah">
<p data-start=3D"1266" data-end=3D"1307">Do not use water inside the opened=
 fuser.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1308" data-end=3D"1367" data-section-id=3D"3x4bss">
<p data-start=3D"1310" data-end=3D"1367">Do not scrape the thermistor with =
a screwdriver or blade.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1368" data-end=3D"1422" data-section-id=3D"1a0vp7x">
<p data-start=3D"1370" data-end=3D"1422">Do not clean the fixing film with =
abrasive material.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1423" data-end=3D"1457" data-section-id=3D"1y81jxx">
<p data-start=3D"1425" data-end=3D"1457">Do not touch the heater element.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1458" data-end=3D"1505" data-section-id=3D"10u0idf">
<p data-start=3D"1460" data-end=3D"1505">Do not bypass the thermostat or th=
ermal fuse.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1506" data-end=3D"1571" data-section-id=3D"5502id">
<p data-start=3D"1508" data-end=3D"1571">Do not repeatedly clear the E002 c=
ode without fixing its cause.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1573" data-end=3D"1894" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-onl=
y-node=3D"">Cleaning helps only when toner contamination causes an incorrec=
t temperature reading. If <strong data-start=3D"1662" data-end=3D"1678">E00=
2 returns</strong>, the ceramic heater, thermistor, thermal fuse, wiring, p=
ower supply, or complete fuser may need replacement. A damaged fixing film=
=E2=80=94wrinkled, torn, or heavily coated=E2=80=94usually requires replace=
ment rather than cleaning.</p></div></div></div></div><div class=3D"z-0 fle=
